1
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:11,050
A photo on a phone is 4 centimetres wide and 3 centimetres tall.

2
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:14,530
You print it 3 times as big, for a frame.

3
00:00:14,580 --> 00:00:16,000
How wide is the print?

4
00:00:16,050 --> 00:00:19,540
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:19,590 --> 00:00:21,590
Multiply the width by 3.

6
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:24,540
4 times 3 is 12 centimetres.

7
00:00:24,590 --> 00:00:29,300
The height is multiplied by 3 as well: 3 times 3 is 9 centimetres.

8
00:00:29,350 --> 00:00:33,170
The print is bigger, but it is the same shape.

9
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:36,890
Remember: 4 times as long means multiply by 4.

10
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:41,390
A line of 2.5 centimetres becomes 10 centimetres.

11
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:45,620
An enlargement changes the size of a shape, but not its shape.

12
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:51,010
Every length is multiplied by the same number, called the scale factor.

13
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:53,820
Rectangle A is 2 squares by 1 square.

14
00:00:53,870 --> 00:00:56,330
It is enlarged by scale factor 3.

15
00:00:56,380 --> 00:00:59,770
Rectangle B is 6 squares by 3 squares.

16
00:00:59,820 --> 00:01:02,860
Think about the corners of the 2 rectangles.

17
00:01:02,910 --> 00:01:08,140
In an enlargement, do the angles stay the same, or are they multiplied too?

18
00:01:08,190 --> 00:01:11,440
Pause the video and decide.

19
00:01:11,490 --> 00:01:13,240
The angles stay the same.

20
00:01:13,290 --> 00:01:15,840
Both rectangles have 4 right angles.

21
00:01:15,890 --> 00:01:18,110
Only the lengths change.

22
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:24,630
To find a scale factor, divide a length on the image by the matching length on the object.

23
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:28,780
A side of 4 centimetres becomes 10 centimetres.

24
00:01:28,830 --> 00:01:30,810
10 divided by 4 is 2.5.

25
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:33,480
The scale factor is 2.5.

26
00:01:33,530 --> 00:01:36,590
An enlarged shape is similar to the original.

27
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:38,380
That means the same shape.

28
00:01:38,430 --> 00:01:42,730
But it is not congruent, because the size is different.

29
00:01:42,780 --> 00:01:43,460
Your turn.

30
00:01:43,510 --> 00:01:46,800
A side of 2 centimetres becomes 7 centimetres.

31
00:01:46,850 --> 00:01:48,610
What is the scale factor?

32
00:01:48,660 --> 00:01:51,970
Pause the video and try it.

33
00:01:52,020 --> 00:01:55,870
Image divided by object: 7 divided by 2 is 3.5.

34
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:58,400
The scale factor is 3.5.

35
00:01:58,450 --> 00:01:59,690
Here is the method.

36
00:01:59,740 --> 00:02:05,850
Step 1: count the length of each side in squares, and multiply by the scale factor.

37
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:11,200
Step 2: start at 1 corner, and draw each side with its new length.

38
00:02:11,250 --> 00:02:13,760
Step 3: keep all the angles the same.

39
00:02:13,810 --> 00:02:18,880
For a slanted side, multiply both the across move and the up move.

40
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:24,380
Step 4: check that every side has been multiplied by the same number.

41
00:02:24,430 --> 00:02:29,730
A right-angled triangle has a base of 3 squares and a height of 2 squares.

42
00:02:29,780 --> 00:02:32,380
Enlarge it by scale factor 3.

43
00:02:32,430 --> 00:02:35,920
The new base is 3 times 3, which is 9 squares.

44
00:02:35,970 --> 00:02:40,160
The new height is 2 times 3, which is 6 squares.

45
00:02:40,210 --> 00:02:41,710
Draw the new triangle.

46
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:47,190
It is 3 times as wide, and 3 times as tall, with the same right angle.

47
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:50,760
A rectangle is 6 centimetres by 4 centimetres.

48
00:02:50,810 --> 00:02:54,730
It is enlarged to 15 centimetres by 10 centimetres.

49
00:02:54,780 --> 00:02:56,990
Find the scale factor.

50
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:58,980
15 divided by 6 is 2.5.

51
00:02:59,030 --> 00:03:05,080
Check with the other pair of sides: 10 divided by 4 is also 2.5.

52
00:03:05,130 --> 00:03:11,550
Both pairs give the same number, so this is an enlargement, with scale factor 2.5.

53
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:15,500
A side of a shape goes 2 squares right and 1 square up.

54
00:03:15,550 --> 00:03:20,140
What happens to it in an enlargement with scale factor 4?

55
00:03:20,190 --> 00:03:22,030
Multiply both moves by 4.

56
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:26,450
The new side goes 8 squares right and 4 squares up.

57
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:30,200
A rectangle 5 by 2 becomes a rectangle 10 by 6.

58
00:03:30,250 --> 00:03:32,590
Is this an enlargement?

59
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:34,380
10 divided by 5 is 2.

60
00:03:34,430 --> 00:03:36,430
But 6 divided by 2 is 3.

61
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:39,360
The 2 numbers are different.

62
00:03:39,410 --> 00:03:39,780
So no.

63
00:03:39,830 --> 00:03:41,810
The shape has been stretched.

64
00:03:41,860 --> 00:03:44,110
It is not an enlargement.

65
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:47,520
Enlarge a rectangle, 3 by 4, by scale factor 2.

66
00:03:47,570 --> 00:03:49,190
Here is Milo's working.

67
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:51,770
Which line goes wrong first?

68
00:03:51,820 --> 00:03:52,890
Line 1 is wrong.

69
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:55,900
A scale factor means multiply every length.

70
00:03:55,950 --> 00:03:57,930
It does not mean add.

71
00:03:57,980 --> 00:04:01,040
3 times 2 is 6, and 4 times 2 is 8.

72
00:04:01,090 --> 00:04:04,070
The new rectangle is 6 by 8.

73
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:07,210
A microscope is an enlargement machine.

74
00:04:07,260 --> 00:04:14,420
With a magnification of 400, a cell 0.02 millimetres wide looks 8 millimetres wide.

75
00:04:14,470 --> 00:04:18,440
When you pinch to zoom on a phone, the picture is enlarged.

76
00:04:18,490 --> 00:04:23,900
Every length grows by the same scale factor, so nothing looks stretched.

77
00:04:23,950 --> 00:04:28,950
A scale factor of 2 makes a photo 2 times as wide and 2 times as tall.

78
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:32,600
So it covers 4 times as much of the screen.

79
00:04:32,650 --> 00:04:33,960
One last question.

80
00:04:34,010 --> 00:04:37,510
A rectangle 3 by 4 becomes a rectangle 9 by 16.

81
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:40,990
Is that an enlargement, or not an enlargement?

82
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:44,430
Pause the video and decide.

83
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:46,370
It is not an enlargement.

84
00:04:46,420 --> 00:04:49,940
9 divided by 3 is 3, but 16 divided by 4 is 4.

85
00:04:49,990 --> 00:04:54,220
The sides are not multiplied by the same number.

86
00:04:54,270 --> 00:04:59,730
To remember: an enlargement multiplies every length by the scale factor.

87
00:04:59,780 --> 00:05:03,860
The angles do not change, so the shape stays the same.

88
00:05:03,910 --> 00:05:09,490
The scale factor is an image length, divided by the matching object length.

89
00:05:09,540 --> 00:05:13,800
On a grid, multiply both the across move and the up move.

90
00:05:13,850 --> 00:05:19,190
Great work! Now practise lesson 14.6 on Camday.
